implementationPlan.description:
New scripts/tests/ci-workflows.test.mjs, plus one comment fix in scripts/tests/usage-receipt.test.mjs.

(1) The test. The dry-run copy is /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-669e/ci-workflows.test.mjs (109 lines, sha256 d51643ce...). It passes on the step 1-2 YAML and kills all 17 mutations tried at edc3e937. Read it and Write it with your editing tool; if it is gone, rebuild it from this spec. It uses node:test, assert/strict and readFileSync only, normalizes CRLF, and reads the files through `new URL('../../.github/workflows/<f>', import.meta.url)`, so a missing file throws instead of passing. It parses by indentation, like the existing CI-reading rows, with no YAML dependency: top-level keys at column 0, jobs at 2, steps `      - ` at 6, step keys at 8, block-run lines at 10+. A step's commands are its trimmed run lines.

LONG holds four commands, each with its OS:
- `node scripts/tests/postflight-safe.mjs bash` (Linux)
- `node scripts/tests/postflight-safe.mjs powershell` (Windows)
- `pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/tests/worktree-landing.ps1` (Windows)
- `node scripts/tests/postflight-safe.mjs pwsh` (Windows)

FAST holds four commands, each with its OS:
- `bash scripts/tests/worktree-landing.sh` (Linux)
- `bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh` (Linux)
- `powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/tests/worktree-landing.ps1` (Windows)
- `pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/tests/parity-check.ps1` (Windows)

The six rows:
- R1 'ci.yml keeps its pull_request and push triggers on main and takes full, ref and artifact-suffix from a caller'. Checks four things:
  - push and pull_request with `branches: [main]`, verbatim;
  - workflow_call inputs exactly {full boolean/false, ref string/'', artifact-suffix string/''};
  - workflow_dispatch inputs exactly {full boolean/true};
  - the concurrency group ends in `-${{ inputs.ref }}`.
- R2 'each long suite runs once, only under inputs.full and on its OS; nothing else waits for the nightly'. Each LONG command has exactly one owning step: build-all-platforms, guard `inputs.full && runner.os == '<OS>'`. The steps whose guard mentions inputs.full number exactly 3, and they hold exactly the LONG commands, plus the LASTEXITCODE stop line.
- R3 'the fast legs of the wrapper suites stay in PR CI on their OS'. Each FAST command has one owning step, in build-all-platforms, with guard exactly `runner.os == '<OS>'`.
- R4 'every checkout takes inputs.ref and every artifact name ends in inputs.artifact-suffix'. At least 5 checkouts, each directly followed by `with:` / `ref: ${{ inputs.ref }}`. At least 5 upload-artifact names, each ending in the suffix.
- R5 'nightly.yml runs on a schedule and on workflow_dispatch with a ref, and calls ci.yml with full: true per ref'. Checks:
  - the header (the text before `on:`) contains "`schedule` only from the default branch";
  - a 5-field cron;
  - workflow_dispatch inputs exactly {ref string/''};
  - exactly one job with `uses:`, and that job has `uses: ./.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `fail-fast: false`, the exact fromJSON matrix line, and `with:` exactly {full: true, ref: ${{ matrix.ref }}, artifact-suffix: -${{ strategy.job-index }}}.
- R6 'PR CI runs this file'. Exactly one step runs `node --test scripts/tests/ci-workflows.test.mjs`: in build-typescript, unguarded.

The 17 mutations killed in planning:
- the bash postflight unguarded;
- postflight-safe added back to the PR step;
- full: false in the nightly;
- one checkout without ref;
- one artifact without the suffix;
- no schedule;
- no workflow_call ref input;
- a fast leg guarded by inputs.full;
- the header without the rule;
- the split-test step removed;
- the nightly calling release.yml;
- the pwsh postflight on Linux;
- concurrency without the ref;
- the pull_request trigger dropped;
- the dispatch ref input renamed;
- a constant suffix;
- the matrix ignoring NIGHTLY_REFS.

This test is how 'a suite moved to the nightly is asserted there': R2 and R5 prove the postflights run under full: true and that the nightly passes it.

(2) usage-receipt.test.mjs:325. Replace the stale line numbers in the G1 comment, which this change shifts, with step names. Change "builds both (ci.yml:222-231) before the step that runs this file (ci.yml:267)." to "builds both (its Build daemon and Build proxy steps) before the step that runs this file (Test agent runtime discovery)." Change nothing else in that file.

approvedScope:
ci.yml:
- on.workflow_call.inputs {full, ref, artifact-suffix} and on.workflow_dispatch.inputs.full;
- the ref suffix on the concurrency group;
- `with: ref` on every checkout and the suffix on every artifact name;
- six steps replacing the three wrapper postflight steps;
- the build-typescript step 'Test the PR and nightly workflow split'.

sourceAssumptions:
GitHub Actions facts the design relies on:
- the inputs context is empty on pull_request and push;
- workflow-level concurrency allows the github, inputs and vars contexts;
- a job that calls a reusable workflow may use strategy, and its with: allows matrix and strategy;
- schedule fires only from the default branch's copy;
- a local `uses: ./.github/workflows/x.yml` runs the caller commit's definition;
- upload-artifact v4+ refuses a duplicate artifact name within one run.
